.TH VC++FILT 1 2026-10-19 "w64devkit" "w64devkit Manual"
.SH NAME
vc++filt \- decode Visual C++ decorated names
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vc++filt
.RB [ \-_ahnp ]
.RI [ symbol ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vc++filt
is
.BR c++filt (1)
for the decorated names produced by Microsoft Visual C++, which begin
with
.BR ? .
It decodes them with the
.B UnDecorateSymbolName
function of the system's DbgHelp library, like MSVC
.BR undname .
.PP
Given
.I symbol
operands,
.B vc++filt
prints the decoded form of each on its own line, and does not read
standard input.
Otherwise it copies standard input to standard output, replacing each
decorated name with its decoded form.
A decorated name is a word that begins with
.B ?\&
and contains
.BR @ ,
made of letters, digits,
.BR _ ,
.BR $ ,
.BR ? ,
.BR @ ,
and non-ASCII bytes.
Other text passes through unchanged, so
.B vc++filt
can filter the output of other tools.
.PP
GCC's mangled names, which begin with
.BR _Z ,
are left alone.
Decode those with
.BR c++filt ,
which can run in the same pipeline.
.SH OPTIONS
Options may be grouped, as in
.BR \-ap .
.B \-\-
ends the options.
.TP
.B \-_
Decode names as 32-bit (x86) names.
This is the default in the x86 kit.
.TP
.B \-a
Include access specifiers, such as
.BR public: .
.TP
.B \-h
Print a usage message on standard output and exit.
.TP
.B \-n
Decode names as 64-bit names.
This is the default in the x64 kit.
.TP
.B \-p
Print only the name, without its type, calling convention, or
parameters.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Invalid option, or an error writing output.
.SH EXAMPLES
Decode a name:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ vc++filt \(aq?f@@YAXPEAH@Z\(aq
void __cdecl f(int * __ptr64)
$ vc++filt \-p \(aq?f@@YAXPEAH@Z\(aq
f
.EE
.RE
.PP
Decode the exports of a DLL built with MSVC:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
$ peports \-e library.dll | vc++filt
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Output to a console is written as UTF-16, so non-ASCII names display
correctly.
Otherwise the output is bytes as read, normally UTF-8.
.PP
The decoded text depends on the version of DbgHelp that comes with
Windows.
A name it cannot decode may be printed unchanged or partly decoded.
Names longer than 65536 bytes pass through unchanged.
.PP
.B \-_
and
.B \-n
are named after the
.B c++filt
options that strip, or keep, a leading underscore, which on Windows
amounts to choosing between 32-bit and 64-bit names.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR c++filt (1),
.BR nm (1),
.BR objdump (1),
.BR peports (1)
